field_worst_run 36
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.8
field_pull_wraps 63
#
# WHAT IT COVERS: a whole stream, cut to what its video shows, on the phase-step lookahead with
# late moves and the refusal. Most of the lock's work sits in the dice game, 2401 s to 2875 s:
# the game hitches once every 4.31 s there, a single 20 to 33 ms gap with no stall, and the
# source phase steps at most of them. Those eight minutes hold 48 of the capture's 66 lookahead
# moves (13 of them late), all 5 lock releases, 24 of the 63 pull wraps, the one tooth-guard
# hold and the worst blend run. The 39 minutes before it are dialog, fades and walking: hitches
# come in short bursts around a stall of 100 ms or more, 85 stalls an hour, and the 376 repeats
# there follow the stalls (375 are holds while the game drew nothing).
# The video is still in the two seconds before most hitches (dialog, a fade to black, the dice
# table): it moves 14% of that time against 45% over the stream, and 34% of the blends land in
# moving footage. A rule that moved blends out of the still stretches and into motion would
# read the same in these counts and look worse on screen.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 44.999 s, from the 2726
# marked frames that open it. It runs 2917.6 s with no holes and shows the game from its first
# frame to its last, so the cut is the video's own span, 45.0 s to 2962.6 s. The game had been
# in its 60 fps regime since 41 s and the source stops at 2967 s. Every second inside the cut
# that falls out of the regime is a single hitch second, so nothing was removed from the middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.9% against 0.8% (0.8% on the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran),
# worst run 38 against 36, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 62 against 63. Counted over
# this window, blends are 1349 against 1348, repeats 403 against 406, skips 180 against 180,
# lock releases 5 against 5 at the same presents, and lookahead moves 67 against 66. The extra
# replay move is at 2426.3 s, where the field refused a step whose first frame sat 2032 us
# ahead of the target, 51 us inside the refusal's cutoff, and the replay saw it just outside.
# The worst run is one event in both, a cancelled step and then a late move at 2579.9 s; the
# field made the late move two presents sooner.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
max_worst_run 38
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 1.3
min_reseeds 97
